      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Storing high volumes of flammable industrial solvents in high-density racking systems is a risky business, and the primary risk factors are as follows: \n\n1. Thermal Runaway: When solvents are stored in high-density racking systems, the risk of thermal runaway increases. This is because the heat generated by the solvents can build up, leading to a rapid increase in temperature. This can cause the solvents to ignite, leading to a fire or explosion. The risk of thermal runaway is exacerbated when the solvents are stored in close proximity to each other, as this can lead to a domino effect, where one solvent igniting can cause others to ignite as well.\n\n2. Fire Suppression Efficacy: The configuration of the racking system can impact the efficacy of fire suppression efforts. For example, if the solvents are stored in a way that makes it difficult for fire suppression systems to reach them, this can make it more difficult to extinguish a fire. Additionally, if the solvents are stored in a way that makes it difficult to evacuate the area, this can also impact the efficacy of fire suppression efforts.\n\n3. Ventilation: Poor ventilation can lead to the buildup of flammable vapors, increasing the risk of fire or explosion. High",
